index 08808b2a..58ed6575 100644
--- a/benchmark/review40/w4-compat/RESULTS.md
+++ b/benchmark/review40/w4-compat/RESULTS.md
@@ -110,6 +110,21 @@ Through the CLI, `-T 1`, 13 files:
   rc3's parse). The 4-thread decompress figure of KLZH2 3 (0.68x of KLZH 3) is one run on a loaded host and is not
   matched by the 1-thread run; it needs the M5.
 
+Decode time split on the landed tree (`benchmark/review40/klzh2/dec_time.c`, 12 Silesia files in 4 MiB blocks,
+best of 9, entropy decode of the streams + sequence loop; raw: `results/dec_time-w4-L1.txt`, `-L3.txt`):
+
+| level | codec 29 | codec 32 | codec 32 / codec 29 time | before the lane (klzh2 RESULTS, section 2) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | 63.8 + 118.4 = 182.1 ms | 79.4 + 143.5 = 222.6 ms | 1.22x | 200.7 and 219.1 ms: 1.09x |
+| 3 | 52.7 + 136.4 = 189.0 ms | 67.9 + 153.7 = 221.6 ms | 1.17x | 213.2 and 231.8 ms: 1.09x |
+
+The lane's decoder work went to codec 29's sequence loop (level 3: 154.3 -> 136.4 ms, refills only when a field
+needs them) and to khuf's tables, which both codecs use (codec 32's streams at level 3: 75.7 -> 67.9 ms, mozilla
+27.4 -> 24.5 ms). Codec 32's loop already refilled once per sequence, so it gained nothing there, and the gap
+between the two decoders widened. **Negative result:** the same conditional refills in codec 32's loop are slower
+(sequence loop of six files at level 3, two rounds: 122.8 and 118.9 ms as it is, 134.8 and 142.6 ms with them);
+not kept.
+
 ## 5. Verification
 
 On `1fe6a718` (the tree with all six lane commits):
